%N A350556 Denominators of Conway's PIGAME.
%C A350556 PIGAME is a FRACTRAN program consisting of 40 fractions, whose denominators are listed here. The fact that the last denominator is a(40) = 1 implies that the successor function A395539 is defined for all integers (in contrast to, e.g., the POLYGAME successor function A400295 where none of the denominators A350664 equals 1). - _M. F. Hasler_, Sep 24 2026
%C A350556 See A350555 for numerators, comments and links.
%e A350556 From _M. F. Hasler_, Sep 16 2026: (Start)
%e A350556 The fractions A350555(n)/a(n) are (365/46, 29/161, 79/575, 679/451, 3159/413, 83/407, 473/371, 638/355, 434/335, 89/235, 17/209, 79/122, 31/183, 41/115, 517/89, 111/83, 305/79, 23/73, 73/71, 61/67, 37/61, 19/59, 89/57, 41/53, 833/47, 53/43, 86/41, 13/38, 23/37, 67/31, 71/29, 83/19, 475/17, 59/13, 41/291, 1/7, 1/11, 1/1024, 1/97, 89/1).
%e A350556 See A395539 for examples how the PIGAME program/successor function is applied to initial values. (End).
%Y A350556 Cf. A000796, A203363, A350555 (numerators), A395539 (the PIGAME successor function).
